resources.string:
%1$s uses Android’s accessibility service (AccessibilityService API).

Why?
To know which icon you tap on your home screen and which app opens. This is what lets the animation start BEFORE the app appears. No other Android feature gives notice early enough.

What the app receives:
• the name written under the icon you tap on the home screen;
• the name of the app that comes to the foreground;
• the home screen’s announcements when you close an app (“app … closed”), so the animation plays again next time.

What the app does NOT do:
• it does not read the content of your screens or what you type (messages, passwords…);
• it never acts on your behalf;
• nothing is collected, stored on a server or shared: everything stays on your phone.

You can turn this service off at any time in Settings > Accessibility.
